    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0696" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg482"/>

                <head>Earl Granville to General Schenck</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 14, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 10th instant, informing me of the appointment of Judge James
                    S. Frazer as a commissioner under Article XII of the treaty of Washington, and I
                    beg leave to thank you for this communication.</p>
                <p>I have at the same time the honor to inform you that Mr. Russell Gurney, recorder
                    of London, has been appointed Her Majesty’s commissioner under the same article
                    of the treaty.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
